From 6fe73239b158cc88cd43b93a5f30f1ca10e00c07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: h0cheung <hcheunh@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:54:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 22/48] remoteproc: qcom: check glink->edge in
 glink_subdev_stop()

For a remoteproc that is doing attach, glink_subdev_start() is only called
once attach has succeeded. If rproc_report_crash() is called from the
attach function, rproc_boot_recovery()->rproc_stop()->glink_subdev_stop()
can run with glink->edge still NULL, causing a NULL pointer dereference in
qcom_glink_smem_unregister().

Bail out early when glink->edge is NULL so qcom_glink_smem_unregister()
is not called if glink_subdev_start() was never called.

Ported from BigfootACA/linux cd72cede17.
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_common.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_common.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_common.c
index 5294e327f..3449aa75e 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_common.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_common.c
@@ -226,6 +226,9 @@ static void glink_subdev_stop(struct rproc_subdev *subdev, bool crashed)
 {
 	struct qcom_rproc_glink *glink = to_glink_subdev(subdev);
 
+	if (!glink->edge)
+		return;
+
 	qcom_glink_smem_unregister(glink->edge);
 	glink->edge = NULL;
 }
